  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-search",
      "text": "Universal search toolkit for DeepSeek Harness — browser-less, GPU-free, works on headless/remote hosts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `search_fetch` | Fetch a URL without a browser, return extracted page text |\n| `search_github` | **First-party GitHub search** (repos / code / issues / commits) — direct GitHub REST API, no Google |\n| `search_corpus_add` | Fetch + extract + chunk + embed + index URLs into an ephemeral SQLite vector corpus |\n| `search_corpus_search` | Semantic top-k search over the corpus (cosine on float32 vectors) |\n| `search_corpus_clear` | Clear the throwaway corpus |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Design",
      "text": "- **TypeScript** (tsc + esbuild build, same pattern as dsh-gitkit; no HTTP framework — native `node:http`)\n- Precompiled regexes, prepared SQLite statements, **float32 BLOB vectors** (4 bytes/dim vs JSON strings), sentence-aware chunking with overlap, batched ARK embeddings (16/batch)\n- Embeddings: ARK `doubao-embedding-large` when `ARK_API_KEY` present (search_code semantic layer; pure-local BM25+rerank core works with **no key and no network**) (`DSH_BROWSER_EMBED_MODEL` overridable); local 64-dim n-gram hash fallback — offline-safe\n- GitHub token: `GITHUB_TOKEN`/`GH_PAT` env or `~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml` refs (line-based parse). Code search requires auth (GitHub rule). Unauthenticated: 10 req/min\n- Optional local HTTP API on native `node:http`: set `DSH_SEARCH_HTTP_PORT` (loopback only):\n  - `GET /health`, `GET /fetch?url=`, `GET /github?q=&type=repo|code|issue|commit`, `POST /corpus {urls}`, `GET /corpus/search?q=&k=`, `DELETE /corpus`\n  - **Auth (v0.5.1, required):** the port alone is no longer enough — also set `DSH_SEARCH_HTTP_TOKEN`\n    (≥16 chars) and every request must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; anything else gets\n    `401` + `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. Port s"
    },
    {
      "section": "GitHub search qualifiers (pass through)",
      "text": "`lang:ts stars:>100`, `repo:owner/name`, `org:google`, `is:issue is:open` — anything the GitHub search API accepts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Search methodology",
      "text": "The plugin ships with a distilled search methodology extracted from 3 professional books (OCR, line-cited):"
    },
    {
      "section": "Search methodology",
      "text": "- [`docs/search-methods.md`](./docs/search-methods.md) — quick reference: operators, engine architecture, investigation workflow, and how each maps to the tools\n- [`docs/book-osint-techniques.md`](./docs/book-osint-techniques.md) — OSINT Techniques 11th: Google/X-Twitter operators, platform lists, recon workflow (110+ items)\n- [`docs/book-ai-powered-search.md`](./docs/book-ai-powered-search.md) — AI-Powered Search: signal boosting, semantic/dense-vector search, ANN, quantization, RRF hybrid ranking (138 items)\n- [`docs/book-bellingcat.md`](./docs/book-bellingcat.md) — We Are Bellingcat: verification workflows, geolocation, disinformation defense (70+ items)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Add `@snow-the/dsh-search` to your profile `dependencies` and `dsh.profile.bundles`, then `pnpm install` + restart."
    }
  ],
